\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Conditional horizon thermodynamics and the finite ledger. (a) The adopted Schwarzschild geometry, Hawking temperature conversion and quarter-area entropy rule give $T_H/T_{\rm  ref}=(M/M_{\rm  ref})^{-1}$ and $S_H/S_{\rm  ref}=(M/M_{\rm  ref})^2$, with both reference quantities evaluated at $M_{\rm  ref}$. (b) The exact entry ledger gives $\Delta E_j/(jk_BT_H)=2/[1+\sqrt  {1-j/N}]$. The continuous curve is an envelope of integer transitions; its value at zero is the differential limit. Extension to complete entry loss is conditional and need not be physically allowed by a formation floor. These analytic curves are neither an emission spectrum nor a newly simulated source result.}}{5}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:c7:scalings}{{1}{5}{Conditional horizon thermodynamics and the finite ledger. (a) The adopted Schwarzschild geometry, Hawking temperature conversion and quarter-area entropy rule give $T_H/T_{\rm ref}=(M/M_{\rm ref})^{-1}$ and $S_H/S_{\rm ref}=(M/M_{\rm ref})^2$, with both reference quantities evaluated at $M_{\rm ref}$. (b) The exact entry ledger gives $\Delta E_j/(jk_BT_H)=2/[1+\sqrt {1-j/N}]$. The continuous curve is an envelope of integer transitions; its value at zero is the differential limit. Extension to complete entry loss is conditional and need not be physically allowed by a formation floor. These analytic curves are neither an emission spectrum nor a newly simulated source result}{figure.caption.31}{}}
